FUN_0000_f98b: faithful reconstruction of the DGROUP:0x36 template-copy service (driver-init helper).

The video driver's init (MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_0009) copies five templates from its own module data into
freshly allocated DGROUP buffers via the engine service DGROUP:0x36 = FUN_0000_f98b (`f98b(count, srcseg,
slot, srcoff)`).  asm 0xf98b:
    push ds ; push ax ; push dx ; push si ; push bx ; mov cx,ds (=DGROUP)
    lcall [DGROUP:0xcc]           ; = FUN_1000_182a : alloc `count` bytes, struct[0]=DGROUP:[slot]=seg
    pop bx ; mov es,[ds:bx]       ; es = allocated segment (just written to DGROUP:[slot])
    xor di,di ; pop si ; pop ds   ; ds = srcseg (pushed dx) ; si = srcoff (pushed si)
    pop cx                        ; cx = count (pushed ax)
    rep movsb ds:si -> es:di      ; copy `count` bytes from srcseg:srcoff to allocseg:0
    mov ax,es ; pop ds ; lret     ; return AX = allocated segment
Ghidra dropped the x86 string-op segment bases (dst es:di collapsed to a bare host offset starting at 0
-> a NULL write -> SIGSEGV, the observed terminal crash of the driver init) AND the allocator's register
args.  Reconstruct faithfully: param_1=count, param_2=srcseg (ABSOLUTE runtime seg -- the driver threads
its MZ-relocated template segment at the call site, patch 035), param_3=slot (DGROUP near offset),
param_4=srcoff.  The alloc goes through the real allocator FUN_1000_182a (bytes->paras->184b->0a31,
patches 025/023) which writes the allocated segment into DGROUP:[slot]; f98b then reads it back and copies.
The signature widens param_3/param_4 from pointer to undefined2 (16-bit near offsets, not host pointers);
f98b has no direct C callers (only the DGROUP:0x36 vector, bypassed by the threaded driver init), so the
fwd decl is updated in lockstep.  Asm-verified base-0 0xf98b.
